# Playtest folder and "approved"

- On first use in a session: if `git config core.hooksPath` is empty, run `tools/dev/install-hooks.ps1` (turns on the pre-commit guard).

- Nathan plays ONLY in `C:\Users\Natha\Documents\boss-rush`.
- Small game changes from Nathan's Cursor sessions: commit straight to `main` and push, like at the start of the project.

## Bigger jobs
- Give them their own branch. Build and check them in boss-rush by default, so Nathan can press F5 right away.
- Switch boss-rush to that branch with `tools/dev/load-pr.ps1 <branch>`. It stashes Nathan's uncommitted edits and re-applies them, keeping the stash as a backup.
- If that would collide with his edits (the script reports a conflict), or he's mid-playtest on a different branch, fall back to a worktree under `C:\Users\Natha\Documents\boss-rush-wt\<branch>`. Never reset or discard his work; the scripts' named, kept stashes are the only stashing allowed. Delete the worktree once its PR is merged or closed.
- Check: `tools/dev/godot-check.ps1`. Need `Godot: 0 errors`.
- Where and how agents run: see `.cursor/rules/agent-runtime.mdc`.

## "approved" / "approve" / "ship it" (boss-rush is on a non-main branch)
1. Run `tools/dev/clean-import-churn.ps1`, then throw away `project.godot` / `default_bus_layout.tres` churn.
2. Run `tools/dev/godot-check.ps1`. If it fails, don't merge. Report it.
3. Merge the branch into `main`, then `git push origin main`.
4. Switch boss-rush back with `tools/dev/back-to-main.ps1`.
5. Delete the branch locally and on origin.
6. Confirm the PR shows as merged.

## "not yet" / "reject"
- Run `tools/dev/back-to-main.ps1`. Keep the branch.

## Always
- Never commit `.cursor/mcp.json` with a literal token (it must say `Bearer ${env:PIXELLAB_API_TOKEN}`), or `.art-ping.env`, `.wrangler/`, `build/` or logs.
- Never push to itch unless Nathan asks.
- Run only one Godot process at a time. Never kill Nathan's Godot.

## Nathan's own Cursor sessions
- Edit boss-rush directly. Nathan presses F5 to test. No branch needed.
- "approved" / "save it" / "ship it" on `main`: run `tools/dev/clean-import-churn.ps1`, then commit and push to origin `main`.
- If boss-rush is on a feature branch when he makes his own edits, commit them onto that branch so they ride along with it.
- Never leave his approved work uncommitted. At the end of any session where he approved changes, everything is committed and pushed.

## "not yet: <reason>" on a feature branch
- Post the reason as a comment on that branch's PR with `gh pr comment` (gh is installed on Cherry).
- If gh isn't available, write it to `design/feedback/<branch>.md`, commit and push to the branch.
- Then switch boss-rush back with `tools/dev/back-to-main.ps1`.

## Screenshots
- Use godot-mcp on Nathan's open editor. It is always the boss-rush folder, so shots match what he plays.

## itch
- Only when Nathan says "publish to itch".
- boss-rush must be on `main`, clean, pushed and in sync with origin.
- Run `tools/dev/godot-check.ps1`. Export the "Web Playtest" preset and `butler push` to `swipe-playtest:html5`. Report the build version.
- Never publish from a feature branch or a dirty folder.

## Pixel's branches
- Cursor (not Pixel) loads Pixel's branches into boss-rush. Follow `.cursor/rules/pixel-handoff.mdc`.
